# Helium · He · gate 2

**Helium** (He) is element **2** of the periodic table — a **noble gas**, period 1, group 18, p-block, gas at standard conditions, atomic weight **4.0026**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Second-most abundant in the cosmos; utterly inert; becomes a frictionless superfluid near absolute zero.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **2** falls on **0:1 — second valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **1**. That state is *the second reach — the diffuse, the airy, the not-quite-held* — the nature of emergence here is **ethereal**. Helium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — ethereal
This emergent carries the **ethereal** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#9a7cff`.

